--
not handled
^warning: ignoring
--
When the definition linked in returns double and the call's declaration
int, link_goto_model makes the call's left-hand side a typecast of the
int variable.  adjust_float_expressions turned it into a floatbv_typecast,
which symex cannot assign to ("l2_rename_rvalues case `floatbv_typecast'
not handled"); with that fixed, symex assigned a plain typecast from double
to int, which the SAT backend does not convert (it needs a rounding
mode), so the variable was unconstrained.  The typecast lvalue is now kept,
and symex assigns `x := (int)result' rounding towards zero (C17 6.3.1.4).
